/-!
# KFM 9c: the per-axis root-table program (`chirpL` recurrence in IL)

The recurrence `g_{k+1} = Q_Δ(g_k h_k)`, `h_{k+1} = Q_Δ(h_k c)` of `KFMTabM.chirpL` is run by
`chirpG pM n`:

* state: `0 = [g.re, g.im] ++ R0`, `pH = [h.re, h.im] ++ RH`, `pK = [c.re, c.im] ++ RK`,
  ruler `2^Δ` on `pR`;
* one iteration `chirpB` copies `g` to the output stack `pV` and replaces `(h, g)` by
  `(Q_Δ(h c), Q_Δ(g h))` with two `entryB` calls (eight `MulOK` products);
* after `n` iterations `pV` holds the entries in reverse order; `revP` moves them in order onto
  `pW`, and the state pairs are dropped.

`chirpG_runs`: `pW = gflat (chirpL Δ c h g n) ++ RW`, everything else restored, at cost
`n (8 φ + 3·10^5 (w + Δ + 1)) + 10^4 (n + 1)(w + 1)` when all states stay within `w` bits.

With `c = oneP Δ` the same program produces the geometric table `geoL` (`geoL_eq_chirpL`).
The state errors (`cst_err`) give the size bound `zsz ≤ Δ + 2` (`zsz_of_near`).
-/

